            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with vomiting and diarrhea].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A1288</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 38-year-old woman was admitted to the emergency department with vomiting, diarrhoea and abdominal pain since four days. She used anticoagulant drugs because of venous thromboembolism. Echography of the abdomen revealed a subcapsular hematoma of the liver. The patient recovered after bloodtransfusion and conservative treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
